WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.426
Hi! Have you noticed that a puppy grows into a dog, and a mango seed grows into a mango tree? Today let's learn about reproduction and inherited traits.

2
00:00:12.576 --> 00:00:17.634
To reproduce means that a living thing produces new young of its own kind.

3
00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:25.266
A mango seed grows into a new mango tree, not an apple tree. And a cat always gives birth to kittens.

4
00:00:25.416 --> 00:00:32.538
Living things grow old and die. Without reproduction, that kind of living thing would slowly die out.

5
00:00:32.688 --> 00:00:39.978
So reproduction makes sure a kind of living thing carries on, generation after generation.

6
00:00:40.128 --> 00:00:48.618
Why do you look like your father or mother? Because parents pass some characteristics to their children. This is called inheritance.

7
00:00:48.768 --> 00:00:55.914
For example, hair colour, whether you have dimples, and the shape of your earlobes are inherited from your parents.

8
00:00:56.064 --> 00:01:01.170
A child may have some characteristics like the father, and others like the mother.

9
00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:09.546
Plants inherit too. Seeds from a plant with red flowers often grow into plants with red flowers.

10
00:01:09.696 --> 00:01:18.546
Not every characteristic is inherited. Swimming, cycling and playing the piano are skills you learn. They are not inherited.

11
00:01:18.696 --> 00:01:23.490
A scar on your knee from a fall will not be passed on to your children either.

12
00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:30.162
Whether you speak Chinese or English is learnt from the people around you. It is not inherited.

13
00:01:30.312 --> 00:01:37.890
Here's a tip: ask yourself, were you born with it, or did you learn it or did it happen later?

14
00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:45.690
Watch out! Some pupils think that if Dad can swim, his baby is born able to swim. That is wrong!

15
00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:52.074
Swimming is a skill learnt later. It cannot be inherited, so the child has to learn it.

16
00:01:52.224 --> 00:01:59.322
Remember: inherited traits are things you are born with, like hair colour or dimples.

17
00:01:59.472 --> 00:02:10.506
Your turn! Speaking English, having dimples, or a scar on the hand: which one is inherited? Pause and think.

18
00:02:10.656 --> 00:02:19.554
The answer is dimples. Speaking English is learnt, and a scar comes from an injury. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:19.704 --> 00:02:29.538
Another one! What would happen if a kind of living thing stopped reproducing? Pause and think.

20
00:02:29.688 --> 00:02:37.938
The old ones would die and there would be no young to replace them, so that kind would die out. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:38.088 --> 00:02:49.170
Last one! A boy's father has curly hair, and the boy has curly hair too. Why? Pause and think.

22
00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:57.858
Because hair type is an inherited characteristic. It was passed on from his father. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:58.008 --> 00:03:10.338
Remember: reproduction keeps a kind of living thing going, generation after generation. Young inherit some characteristics from their parents, but learnt skills and scars are not inherited.

24
00:03:10.488 --> 00:03:16.218
Go into your garden and find young plants that look like their parents!

